# Forge — Local-First AI IDE

## Mission
Desktop IDE fork of VS Code (base: voideditor/void), purpose-built for **local LLM inference only**. No cloud API keys. All AI features talk to localhost model servers (Ollama, LM Studio, llama.cpp, vLLM, LocalAI, etc.).

**Non-negotiables:** No telemetry, no accounts, no license gating, no cloud provider paths. Network only for Open VSX marketplace, optional self-hosted updates, and localhost/LAN model traffic.

## Build Phases (run sequentially, one Agent session each)

| Phase | Goal |
|-------|------|
| 0 | Scaffold: clone Void, baseline build, rebrand product.json + Open VSX |
| 1 | Strip cloud providers, telemetry, Microsoft marketplace, Void update feed |
| 2 | `ILocalProvider` layer + auto-discovery + health dots |
| 3 | Chat (Cmd+L) + inline edit (Cmd+K) via providers |
| 4 | Agent, tools, checkpoints, Fast-Apply, lint-feedback |
| 5 | Tab autocomplete (FIM) |
| 6 | Skills system (`.forge/skills/*/SKILL.md`) |
| 7 | Model/provider UI + hardware-aware fit |
| 8 | Performance pass (<2.5s cold start, <400MB idle RAM) |
| 9 | Packaging (signed macOS DMG, Windows, Linux) |

## Target Code Layout (rename void → forge over phases)

```
src/vs/workbench/contrib/forge/
├── browser/          # React UI, chat, autocomplete, edit
├── common/           # ILocalProvider, skills, settings, prompts
└── electron-main/    # HTTP to localhost, MCP, hardware probe
```

## Provider Defaults

| Runtime | Host:Port |
|---------|-----------|
| Ollama | localhost:11434 |
| LM Studio | localhost:1234 |
| llama.cpp | localhost:8080 |
| vLLM | localhost:8000 |
| LocalAI | localhost:8080 |

## Acceptance Checklist
- Zero network except localhost pings + Open VSX
- E2E chat/agent/autocomplete on Ollama, LM Studio, llama.cpp
- Agent refuses gracefully when `supportsTools === false`
- Skills hot-reload with selective injection
- No Void/Microsoft branding or telemetry in product.json

See full spec in project docs or upstream conversation for detailed interfaces (`ILocalProvider`, `IModelCapabilities`, skills format).
